  "scientific_interpretation": {
    "micro_ego_head_fidelity": "Translation MAE: 0.0272m, Rotation MAE: 0.0425rad. Crucially, on zero latent delta (Delta s = 0 during blackout), micro_ego_head outputs static bias [0.012910539284348488, 0.0013786181807518005, 0.00013427063822746277]. It cannot perceive robot motion under black-frame dropouts.",
    "replay_resolution": "Under same-trajectory replay, full learned memory achieves blackout error 0.7047m. Zeroed ego motion achieves 0.7082m. Frozen pre-blackout memory achieves 0.6727m. Oracle odometry achieves 0.5581m.",
    "mechanism_verdict": "The learned micro_ego_head fails to provide an accurate egocentric coordinate update during visual blackout. The fixed 0.65/0.35 blending exponentially decays valid memory into static black-frame noise (0.35^10 ~ 2.7e-5). Frozen memory and donor injection beat full memory not because they model ego-motion, but because they prevent decay into black-frame garbage."
